      "body": "## Motivation\n\n```bash\npython3 -m pytest test/registered/attention/unittests/dsv4/test_deepseek_v4.py -k TestLateLayerTailRequestIndices\n```\n\nWith `--enable-decoder-swa-bounded-replay`, every extend forward runs `_build_late_layer_tail_metadata`, which calls `torch.repeat_interleave(req_pool_indices, tail_lens)` with device repeat counts and no `output_size`. PyTorch then copies the total to the host to size the output: one device synchronization per extend forward, although the tail lengths are already on the host (`tail_lens_cpu`).\n\n## Modifications\n\nAdds `_repeat_per_request(values, counts, counts_cpu)`, which passes `output_size=sum(counts_cpu)`, and uses it for the tail request indices.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe output is the same by construction. `TestLateLayerTailRequestIndices` (new) runs the helper under `torch.cuda.set_sync_debug_mode(\"error\")` and checks its values. `test_deepseek_v4.py`: 26 passed (45 subtests) on GB300.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot benchmarked; it removes one host synchronization per extend forward on the decoder-SWA bounded replay path.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37819852511](https://g